Oh, giants are so stupid ceatures, that they probably see a chest as a kind
of small boulder (not worth picking up and hurling ;-) Now, the Wizard is
another problem (well, maybe he knows already what he put in every chest in
the dungeon...?) ;-)
  Seriously: You have to be a bit careful with that feature, it will change
the game balance slightly. For now the chests you find are untouched, with
such addition most chests you find will be looted already, the traps on them
already disarmed... Some 'placed chests' (like those in throne rooms) will
not have any sense any more (you enter the throne room and the monsters rush
to open the chest? Why didn't they do it earlier?). Maybe a good idea would 
be to give the ability to a few monster classes (hobbits, elves, nymphs, 
giants?) - this will reduce the usefulness of chests as 'permanent sinks'
for unused but dangerous items - but at the same time will not change too
much in the present situation...
